WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Habits are repeated behavior patterns supported by cues, actions, and consequences.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.955
A cue makes the behavior more likely to start.

00:00:06.955 --> 00:00:08.700
The action is the behavior itself.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.640
The consequence, whether obvious or subtle,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.520
influences whether the pattern is likely to repeat.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.010
Over time,

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:18.180
repeated cue-behavior-consequence patterns can become easier to trigger and perform.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.455
This is one reason relying only on willpower is fragile.

00:00:20.455 --> 00:00:22.370
A person may intend to behave differently,

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.280
but the environment keeps triggering the old pattern.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.815
If the phone is visible, the distraction is one tap away.

00:00:27.815 --> 00:00:30.940
If the checklist is buried, the desired behavior takes extra effort.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.900
If the team rewards speed but not quality,

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.250
rushed work may become the path of least resistance.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.600
Environment design changes the pattern by changing friction.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.920
Reduce friction for desired behaviors and increase friction for distractions or unwanted

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.680
patterns.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.410
Put the practice material where it is easy to start.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.920
Make the next step visible.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.760
Remove avoidable cues for behaviors that interrupt focus.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.255
Use routines that make the desired action more automatic,

00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:54.384
especially at the start of a session.

00:00:54.384 --> 00:00:57.400
Replacing patterns is usually more practical than only suppressing them.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.865
Instead of saying, stop procrastinating, define the cue and the replacement action.

00:01:00.865 --> 00:01:03.880
When I open the project folder, I write the next visible step.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.800
When I finish a meeting, I capture one decision and one follow-up.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.780
Neuroplasticity supports habit change over time, but the change needs repetition,

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.950
feedback, and a system that makes the new behavior easier to repeat.
